{
    "background_story": "Theodora was a free-spirited artist who defied conventions. Growing up in a family of bookworms, she was the only one who never took to reading or writing. While her parents and siblings spent hours devouring classics, Theodora would rather spend her time exploring the outdoors or experimenting with paint. Her lack of interest in literature was met with concern, but Theodora didn't let it define her. Instead, she channeled her energy into creating vibrant, abstract art pieces that spoke to people on a deeper level. Her art studio became a haven for like-minded individuals who shared her passion for the unconventional. Theodora's unliterary nature allowed her to tap into a unique creative voice, one that resonated with those who valued experience over words.",
